WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.820
Oh, we have new polling data from the 2020
Democratic primary.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.810
The data is good for Joe Biden.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:12.019
It's good for Elizabeth Warren and it's actually
not so good for Bernie Sanders.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:16.900
And I know people are sick of me saying this,
but I'm not supporting Joe Biden.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.460
I am merely telling you what the polling data
says.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:25.769
I did a story earlier this week saying, hey,
Biden in his first 24 hours raised more money

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:30.789
than anybody else in the 2020 Democratic primary
in the first 24 hours.

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:35.210
And he did it from fewer donors with a larger
average donation.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:39.989
And I got a ton of emails and tweets and comments
saying, David, why are you shilling for Joe?

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:42.520
I'm just reporting to you what the numbers
are.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.520
Okay.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.520
And likewise, I'm reporting to you that we
have new polling data that is from after Joe

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.870
Biden announced that he's running for president.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:51.870
Okay?

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:58.880
The morning consult tracking poll, which surveys
500 registered voters weekly has Biden up

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.770
to 36% support since he announced his candidacy.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:13.290
This is among Democratic primary voters nationally,
Biden at 36% Bernie in second place with 22%

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:19.920
and Elizabeth Warren also actually getting
a bit of a bump up to 9% she was in like three

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.140
to 5% in a lot of Poles for awhile.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.320
She's now more intellect, the six to 12 range
depending on which poll you look at.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.740
Uh, so she's rising and this is not the best
news for Bernie Sanders.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:36.380
Bernie Sanders still very, very strongly in
second place, but Bernie had actually been

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.829
pulling as high as the mid to high twenties.

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:43.030
He's now down to 22% and even lower in some
recent polls.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.950
So he's suffered in the last seven to 10 days,
but still a very solid second place and there's

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.680
a very long time to go.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.210
Whether you're in first, second, or third
place right now, even fourth place, you can

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:58.100
make the argument still all very well positioned
to ultimately take the lead.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.670
But you know who this is all really bad for
its other establishment Democrats.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:07.079
The day that Joe Biden announced last week,
I told you this isn't good for Kamala Harris.

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:09.240
This isn't good for Beto O'rourke.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:14.420
Anybody who is playing the more moderate centrist
role in the Democratic primary, it's not good

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:19.530
that Biden has announced he is going to consolidate
the establishment sort of center left vote

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.460
and it's being out to a tee.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:29.360
Camela Harris had been previously a polling
as high as 15 in February, sort of bounced

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.290
around between 10 and 13 since then.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:37.850
Camilla Harris is now down to just eight in
a recent Quinnipiac poll down to seven in

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:43.490
the recent morning consult poll Beto or Rourke,
he had actually been polling as high as 11

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:44.730
in mid to late March.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:51.160
Beto is down to between four and six in the
most recent four-poles Biden's announcement

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.420
has not been good for Beto and then sort of
unaffected by Biden running are a whole bunch

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.650
of people who are still polling as low as
zero and as high as two.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.960
Uh, Andrew Yang got up to three in one poll.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.140
Recent polls haven't met either one or two.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:09.730
Uh, who Leanne Castro is basically at 1% across
the board.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:13.650
Tulsi Gabard actually pulled zero in the last
Quinnipiac poll.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:17.890
Got a 1% in the last morning consult poll.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:24.160
And as I've said before, um, several months
ago we were at a point where the polling was

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.810
not yet accurately indicative of who is likely
to really be in the running.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.490
By the time the primaries get going.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:31.980
It was a little early.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.930
We're now kind of starting to get into the
pre summer phase.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.580
Um, at which point the polls do start to give
us a hint as to who's a contender.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:45.401
And we're starting to see this four way may
be five way race, Bernie, uh, sorry, in, in

00:03:45.401 --> 00:03:52.510
descending order, Biden, Bernie Warren, Budaj
edge and maybe Kamala Harris, if she can consolidate

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:58.370
some of that non Biden sort of establishment
centrus support doesn't mean things can't

00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:59.370
change.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:03.630
We're just now starting to see who seems to
be completely unable to get traction and who

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:07.170
is emerges emerging as this kind of a, a leaderboard.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:10.360
And we'll see by June 1st I think we're actually
going to have a much more solid idea of what

00:04:10.360 --> 00:05:50.259
a, what it's looking like.

